            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0617" n="613" xml:id="pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">651G.11251/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hong Kong</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Southard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hong
                                Kong</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1938-12-22"
                            >December 22, 1938</date>.<lb/>[Received December 22—12:20
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following telegram has been received from the American Consul at Saigon.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“December 22, 11 a.m. Restrictions on transit automobiles and trucks by road
                        from French Indo-China into China removed by order of the Governor General
                        made known orally last night. Only transit and registration taxes
                        required.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking, Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Southard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
